error[E0277]: `{integer}` is not a kernel value
 --> tests/ui/integer_counter.rs:7:5
  |
7 |     while y > 1.0 {
  |     ^^^^^ the trait `Value<'_>` is not implemented for `{integer}`
  |
  = note: kernel loops, kernel branches and outputs hold `Real`, `Cplx` and `Mask` values (`f64`, `Complex<f64>`, `bool` in a `#[kernel]` function), or tuples or arrays of them; a counter updated in a kernel loop must be a float (`let mut i = 0.0`)
  = help: the following other types implement trait `Value<'k>`:
            ()
            (A,)
            (A, B)
            (A, B, C)
            (A, B, C, D)
            (A, B, C, D, E)
            (A, B, C, D, E, F)
            (A, B, C, D, E, F, G)
          and $N others
  = note: required for `(Real<'_>, {integer})` to implement `Value<'_>`
  = note: required for `symjit::kernel::Mask<'_>` to implement `LoopCond<'_, (Real<'_>, {integer})>`
